            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to stay alive, then the Marathi for to wobble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मृदू",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मृदू — mṛdū — \"soft-hearted; gentle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आमच्या शिक्षिका स्वभावाने मृदू आहेत. āmcyā śikṣikā svabhāvāne mṛdū āhet. Our teacher is gentle by nature."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Unchanging: मृदू (mṛdū) आवाज, a gentle voice. Sanskrit writes the word with a short final vowel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मृदू (mṛdū) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit mṛdu, \"soft, weak\" (CDIAL 10292), with the final vowel lengthened as Marathi writes it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
